# CincaiAndroid
A *cincai* Android fork based on LineageOS, built with love, duct tape, and sarcasm.

---

## Release Channels

| Label               | Stage             | Description                                                                 |
| ------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **cincai**          | Stable            | 💎 Official release. Tested, polished, and safe for your in-laws' phones.   |
| **almost cincai**   | Release Candidate | 🧪 Almost there. Good enough for daily use, but might still randomly vibe.  |
| **too cincai**      | Beta              | 🐛 Expect some weirdness. We're experimenting... with feeling.              |
| **hardcore cincai** | Development       | 💥 Enter at your own risk. This is where dragons and dirty logs live.       |
| **peak-cincai**     | Bleeding Edge     | 🚀 When this shows up, it means a **major version upgrade** is incoming.    |

---

## Getting Started

To start building CincaiAndroid (based on LineageOS), you’ll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).
## 🛠 Preparing Your Fedora

Before you can start cincai-ing your Android build, make sure Fedora is ready to rumble.

~~~

### 1. Install Build Essentials
---
You can do this the short cincai way:

```bash
sudo dnf install @c-development @development-tools
---
Or, for the more ceremonial Fedora fans:

sudo dnf group install "C Development Tools and Libraries" "Development Tools"
---
### 2. Install Additional Required Packages

These are not optional. Missing one = hours of head-scratching.

sudo dnf install --skip-unavailable \
android-tools \
ccache \
clang \
cmake \
git-lfs \
gperf \
lzop \
maven \
meson \
pngcrush \
rpm-build \
schedtool \
dpkg-dev \
libstdc++ \
ncurses-compat-libs \
python3-mako \
python3-networkx \
syslinux-devel \
openssl-devel-engine \
libxcrypt-compat

✅ --skip-unavailable is used just in case some packages aren't in your enabled repos. But ideally, keep your repos fresh.

3. Setup Your Workspace

mkdir -p ~/bin ~/android

4. Get the repo Tool

Download and install Google’s repo tool (replace ... with actual URL):

curl https://storage.googleapis.com/git-repo-downloads/repo > ~/bin/repo
chmod a+x ~/bin/repo


### 5. Repo Initialization
---
```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/dmmartin/leandroid.git -b cincai-dev --git-lfs


6. Sync the Source


