🧻 Side Note for Ubuntu Users

If you're on Ubuntu... just don't. Save yourself the emotional damage.
Fedora is the cincai-approved build distro — for a reason.
⚠️ A Word to the Ubuntu Mouse-Click Warriors

    "What’s wrong with Ubuntu??"

Ohhh nothing much... except:

    Compiler versions often outdated

    Missing newer build tools unless you manually add obscure PPAs

    Python versions weirdly bundled or symlinked wrong

    Permissions cursed

    Half your time goes into fixing things Fedora just installs right

Ubuntu is great — for web browsing, opening VSCode, or watching anime.
But for Android ROM building?

    ❌ No. Don't do it.

🩹 Save yourself. Use Fedora.

Fedora has:

    Fresh toolchains

    Logical package naming

    No weird surprises in /usr/bin/python

    Less tribal StackOverflow copy-pasting

So before you go full “why isn’t this working???”... just:

sudo dnf install life

🧨 Ubuntu Disclaimer
🙅‍♂️ Ubuntu? Not Recommended.

If you still insist on using Ubuntu — despite the warnings, the signs, and the ancient curses —
please know the following:

    You’re on your own.

    The dev team officially recommends Mageia over Ubuntu.

        Yes. We said Mageia.

    If Mageia also feels too advanced for you...

        🧸 Please consult the Ubuntu forums.

        🧙 Our devs are not trained in handling apt-induced trauma.

We repeat:

    🛑 We take zero responsibility for crashes, curses, or random repo failures on Ubuntu.


